    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0556" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1005</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-10T16:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 10, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.12 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My December 6, 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>] p.m. With reference to
                    proposed Pan-American congress I understand that the Peruvian Minister has three
                    times told the President that the Governments of Peru, Bolivia, Uruguay, and
                    Ecuador would not be represented at such a congress unless it were called for
                    the avowed purpose of breaking relations with Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
